# —— Supabase auth (optional; local device auth works without these) ——
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key
# See docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md for the profiles SQL.

# Optional. After deploying worker/:
# VITE_API_BASE=https://thumbric-api.YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev

# Custom domain (set in Pages workflow after thumbric.ai DNS is live):
# VITE_BASE_PATH=/
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://thumbric.ai/

# —— Premium AI imaging (fal.ai Flux Schnell) ——
# Preferred: keep the key on the Worker, never in the client.
#   cd worker && npx wrangler secret put FAL_KEY
#   then build the site with VITE_API_BASE pointing at that Worker.
# VITE_API_BASE=https://thumbric-api.YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
#
# Local-only escape hatch (insecure — the key is baked into the JS bundle):
# VITE_FAL_KEY=your_fal_key_here
#
# Without either, the AI maker shows “Free preview engine” and uses free
# Pollinations (+ studio fallback looks). Free path is never broken by missing keys.
#
# With Worker + FAL_KEY, the maker shows “Pro imaging ready” (see GET /api/ai/ready).
# Photoreal Canva-grade faces need FAL_KEY on the Worker + VITE_API_BASE on Pages.
#
# Full setup notes: docs/AI_IMAGING_SETUP.md
#
# —— Gemini / Nano Banana (master doc §2–3) ——
# Not wired yet. Do not set GEMINI_API_KEY expecting the SPA to use it today.
# Future: server-side only on the Worker; never VITE_ Gemini keys in the client.
